module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.carrier_by_spelling

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data carrier_by_spelling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "carrier_by_spelling" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**carrier by spelling** (INVALID STATE: a module imports the structural text carrier `v2.std.text` `String` and then authors a BARE `String` as if that import bound it; KERNEL NAMES ARE NEVER OVERRIDDEN BY IMPORTS (`v1.compiler.infer_env` `overlay_skips_kernel_name`, kernel overlay unconditional since #9813), so the bare spelling binds the KERNEL host carrier beside the unused import.",

    "A host-carrier value can therefore flow into a fold whose declared positions are the STRUCTURAL carrier, and the front end ACCEPTS the program.",

    "HARM: section 5 silent wrongness on the source path, becoming a TARGET compiler refusal on the emitted-Rust path -- gunbc says Accepted and hands over a crate rustc will not compile.",

    "THE SPECIMEN, measured on the `v2.compiler.compile` / `00_compile` closure rather than on a fixture: `gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier` `receipt_2_66765317_raw_error_diagnostic_identities` carries the parse.rs pair `src/v2_compiler_parse.rs` E0282 `type annotations needed` and E0308 `mismatched types`, together with the rest of that census's fifteen identities (lexing, qualified_name, target_model, dag/python/typescript language modules, interpreter `row_key`).",

    "THE FIFTEEN HAND CONVERSIONS are `285b02eed2944331574330282fc49165a805b75e` (`Clear the remaining XL-N closure errors at source: carrier conversions at the boundaries`): each site converted at a construction or operation boundary -- `chars()` ingress, host-carrier `string_length` / `char_at` instead of routing through structural `string_is_empty`, nested `concat` instead of a method on the host token -- so the emitted crate went cargo-clean.",

    "Those conversions are a WORKAROUND POPULATION, not a climb: they leave the competing bindings writable, and the next module that imports `v2.std.text` `\{ String \}` and spells a bare `String` repeats the class. Filed beside `unmarked_workaround` rather than as a specimen of it, because the conversions DID mark their dissolve-on in the frontier receipt; the class they paper over is the binding, not the missing marker.",

    "THE POSITIVE CONTROL THAT MAKES THE BINDING A FACT RATHER THAN A GUESS is already enrolled: `test.claim.self_host_structural_text_witness_test` `w_bare_string_with_text_import_stays_host_deterministically` compiles a module that imports `v2.std.text` `\{ String \}` and returns a literal from a bare `String` boundary, and requires the HOST spelling (a `.to_string()` render) rather than the scalar-sequence elaboration.",

    "That row pins CURRENT kernel-wins; it is the discriminating evidence that the import does not bind, not a claim that kernel-wins is the terminal architecture.",

    "THE VERDICT THAT WAS INVERTED AND CORRECTED, cited so this row does not re-invert it: `gunbc.rust_source_type_bindings` `checkpoint_row_migration_rows` String arm. It previously argued that a module importing `v2.std.text` `String` made every bare `String` the text carrier and the kernel spelling unreachable. The opposite holds. Locals beat kernel; IMPORTS DO NOT.",

    "Three routes, all sound for that checkpoint: a bare reference in an importing module IS the kernel and IS that row's binding; a bare reference INSIDE `v2.std.text` resolves locally and is gated structural; a QUALIFIED `v2.std.text.String` resolves through the alias onto `std.algebra.FreeMonoid` and matches no bare row.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when an emitted type error names `String` at a site whose source module imports `v2.std.text` `\{ String \}`, ask which declaration the BARE spelling resolved to BEFORE asking which conversion is missing. If it resolved to the kernel, the defect is this class and a conversion at the call is treating the symptom.",

    "THE NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT, named so an append does not fork them. `meaning_fork` is the one-name/two-meanings dual this specimen inhabits -- one spelling, kernel versus structural, across scopes -- and remains the general class; this row is the AUTHORING ILLUSION that an import selects the structural arm of that fork for the bare spelling. `generated_binding_shadows_bare_render` is EMISSION composing a use-line with a bare render; here the wrong declaration is already bound in the typed tree. `alias_resolution_collides_with_kernel_spelling` is an INSTRUMENT attributing a QUALIFIED alias to the kernel; here the bare spelling really is the kernel and the instrument that says so (`carrier_realization_census` at declaration_field) is correct. `one_refusal_two_destinations` is two producers rendering two expected types for one column; this class can be one of the reasons those types differ, but the invalid state here is acceptance-then-uncompilable-target, not a misdirected refusal. `accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target` is the shared SYMPTOM class (Accepted source, rustc refuses); this row is the mechanism that produced that symptom for the fifteen-identity population, so it is added rather than absorbed -- repairing any one conversion, or component (iv) of that row, leaves the next bare-spelled import authorable. The declared drop `gunbc.rung_drop` `text_boundary_identity_wall` is leaf-name COMPAT admitting a kernel VALUE at an already-structural BOUNDARY; this class is that the BOUNDARY ITSELF was authored as bare `String` intending the import.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder on the source-acceptance path -- the competing bindings are Accepted, nothing at the .dag boundary is typed, located or countable about the unused import -- and mitigatable on the emitted-Rust self-host path, where rustc E0282/E0308 stop the crate. Section 4b's current rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths, so the class sits below the ladder.",

    "CEILING: 4, structurally impossible. Membership is decidable: a spelling is either a kernel name or it is not, and a resolving scope either has one binding for it or it has two. A constructor roster that admits at most one binding per spelling per scope makes the unused-import-beside-kernel-bare-spelling state unwritable. No undecidable predicate is involved.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, phrased as the capability rather than an artifact: ONE BINDING PER SPELLING PER RESOLVING SCOPE for every kernel homonym that also has a structural declaration, sufficient that `import v2.std.text \{ String \}` either makes a bare `String` the text carrier or REFUSES the import as colliding with a kernel name -- so a host-carrier value cannot inhabit a position the author spelled as the imported type.",

    "A trigger naming the fifteen conversions, the parse.rs pair, the enrolled host-control witness, or a climb of `text_boundary_identity_wall` is less than the capability and would retire this row while the next importing module can still author the class. Repairing a call site, qualifying one annotation, or converting at construction satisfies none of it.)",

    "THE TWO COMPILERS NOW GIVE OPPOSITE ANSWERS FOR THE SAME SOURCE (2026-09-30, gunbc#12760, neat-boar-16's ruling, decision A; flagged by royal-newt-820). In v2, resolve binds a String declaration the author reached by import to THAT declaration: `import v2.std.text \{ String \}` makes a bare `String` the structural carrier (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_kernel_type_foreign_declaration`, ForeignDeclarationBinds). The kernel host text (`v2.std.node` `String`) applies only where no String declaration is visible. That is this row's trigger capability, reached on the v2 source path and pinned by `v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation` `bla_imported_structural_string_binds_its_declaration`. v1 still binds the kernel (`overlay_skips_kernel_name`, pinned by `w_bare_string_with_text_import_stays_host_deterministically`).",

    "SO THE CLASS IS NOW ALSO A MEANING FORK ACROSS THE TWO COMPILERS, and neat-boar-16 ruled where it resolves: AT THE IMPORTERS, NOT THE RULE. Decision A stands, because an import the compiler silently ignores is the defect (a DESIGN section 3 nickname), for the same reason #12512 deleted the std.string_type importers. Every v2.std.text String importer is classified. A HOST-USING importer, which treats its values as host text, has String deleted from its import list, and v1 and v2 then agree (the kernel binds). A STRUCTURAL-USING importer keeps the import, as a DECLARED v1/v2 divergence: v1's answer is wrong but frozen (`gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing` `v1_seed_standing`), and no self-host equivalence is claimed over those modules. THE INSTRUMENT AND THE POPULATION (review 73214 on #12760; census by royal-lark-857, gunbc#12840 at census revision 7b87f99f0a4, after neat-boar-16's fixpoint ruling). The instruments are `v2.lens.text_string_importer_census` `verdict_with_crossings` (a pure .dag reader over each importer's raw parse) and `text_string_importer_fixpoint`. The identity join closes: 407 modules with an import edge into v2.std.text, which are 391 String importers plus 16 non-members, with none missing, extra or duplicated. THE STRUCTURAL-USING POPULATION, the declared divergence, is 15 modules: v2.compiler.self_host.generation, v2.compiler.staged_front_end, v2.lens.fn_index_depth_agreement, v2.lens.realization_vocabulary_containment, v2.test.complexity_gate.source_bridged_pipeline_bridge, v2.test.claim.enforcement.skeleton_call_route_witness, v2.test.execution.self_host_candidate_generation_stage_verdicts, v2.test.manual.fold_source, v2.test.claim.match_arm_binder_frame, v2.test.parse.supplied_token_stream_support, v2.test.tokenize.string_literal_raw_newline, v2.test.compiler.pipeline.stage_bridge, v2.test.floor_cost_debt_edit, v2.test.std_text.carrier_claims, v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt_edit. Eight of them are structural only because they pass host text into a parameter of a module that keeps its import. Two more modules are NAMED DIVERGENCE SITES under ruling 1 (v2.compiler.tokenize, v2.std.integer), and 10 modules that v2 cannot parse keep the import under ruling 4. It is a LOWER BOUND, not a closed set: 24 importers are still undecided and are listed on #12840. The ORDER is enforced where it can be: #12760, which flips the binding, is held as a DRAFT until #12840 and the import-deletion PR have landed. The rung stays the minimum across in-scope paths (the v1 path, below the ladder), and the trigger must hold on BOTH compilers.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "overlay_skips_kernel_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.rust_source_type_bindings", decl_name: "checkpoint_row_migration_rows", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.self_host_structural_text_witness_test", decl_name: "w_bare_string_with_text_import_stays_host_deterministically", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier", decl_name: "receipt_2_66765317_raw_error_diagnostic_identities", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_imported_structural_string_binds_its_declaration", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
